kvarn-varlen: trace, replay or reset the DFlash2 adaptive verify length (V2 runner).

Research experiment for the kvarn-varlen item (docs/research/deepinfer/README.md, "Blocker
for E"; single-user/start_qwen.sh, the VLLM_DFLASH2_LOOKUP_ADAPTIVE comment). NOT in
patches/series. Written against the image's installed (already patched) vLLM 0.31.0.

Adds v1/kvv_sched.py and two calls around DFlash2Speculator.next_num_draft_tokens() in
GPUModelRunner.sample_tokens. All knobs default off; with them unset both calls return at
once and the speculator's decision passes through untouched.

  VLLM_KVV_TRACE=<file>        JSON line per step: request ids, tokens scheduled the step
                               that just ran (its verify length), tokens emitted, the
                               controller state and the next length asked/used (syncs).
  VLLM_KVV_REPLAY=<file>       per new request, force the k-th post-first-token verify
                               decision to the k-th entry of the file (draft counts as the
                               controller returns them, "7,7,15,..."; verify = count + 1),
                               single-request batches only (syncs).
  VLLM_KVV_RESET_ON_NEW_REQ=1  candidate fix for hypothesis H1: a request joining the batch
                               does not inherit the previous request's adaptive state
                               (_prev_want, _sticky, pending flag copy). Host-only.

--- a/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
+++ b/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
@@ -2261,7 +2261,12 @@
                 # Lookup-augmented drafting proposes a long block only while the request
                 # is reproducing its context; the rest of the time it asks the scheduler
                 # to verify the drafter's own (much cheaper) block.
+                # kvarn-varlen experiment (v1/kvv_sched.py): inert unless a VLLM_KVV_* knob is set.
+                from vllm.v1 import kvv_sched
+
+                kvv_sched.before(self.speculator, input_batch)
